--TEST--
A hooked property whose stored value is read needs a value, as a plain property does: a constructor assigns it, and each `set` hook stores it on every path — `rule:classes/definite-property-initialization`, `rule:classes/property-hooks`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Box {
    public int $n = 1;
}

// Compiles: the `get` hook computes the value, so nothing is stored.
class Computed {
    public int $base = 2;
    public int $double {
        get => $this->base * 2;
    }
}

// Compiles: the constructor assigns the property, and the hook always stores it.
class Clamped {
    public int $level {
        set (int $v) {
            if ($v < 0) {
                $this->level = 0;
            } else {
                $this->level = $v;
            }
        }
    }

    public function constructor(int $start) {
        $this->level = $start;
    }
}

// Refused: there is no constructor, so nothing assigns the property.
class NoConstructor {
    public Box $box {
        set (Box $v) {
            $this->box = $v;
        }
    }
}

// Refused: the hook stores the value only when it is positive.
class Sometimes {
    public int $count {
        set (int $v) {
            if ($v > 0) {
                $this->count = $v;
            }
        }
    }

    public function constructor() {
        $this->count = 1;
    }
}

// Refused: the `get` hook reads the stored value, and nothing assigns it.
class Cached {
    public Box $box {
        get => $this->box;
    }
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0409]: `$box` has no default value, and `NoConstructor` declares no constructor to assign it
%A
error[E0409]: the `set` hook of `$count` does not store a value on every path
%A
error[E0409]: `$box` has no default value, and `Cached` declares no constructor to assign it
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
